articles.content_en:
Article 1 A civil relation that falls under any of the following circumstances may be determined by the People's Court as a foreign-related civil relation:
(1) one or both parties are foreign citizens, foreign legal persons or other organizations, or stateless persons;
(2) the habitual residence of one or both parties is outside the territory of the People's Republic of China;
(3) the subject matter is located outside the territory of the People's Republic of China;
(4) the legal facts that produce, change or terminate the civil relation occur outside the territory of the People's Republic of China;
(5) other circumstances that may be determined as foreign-related civil relations.

Article 8 The People's Court shall determine as mandatory provisions as prescribed in Article 4 of the Law of the People's Republic of China on the Application of Laws to Foreign-Related Civil Relations the provisions of laws and administrative regulations that fall under any of the following circumstances, involve the public interest of the People's Republic of China, cannot be excluded by agreement of the parties, and are directly applicable to foreign-related civil relations without the guidance of conflict rules:
(1) provisions concerning the protection of workers' rights and interests;
(2) provisions concerning food or public health safety;
(3) provisions concerning environmental safety;
(4) provisions concerning financial safety such as foreign exchange control;
(5) provisions concerning anti-monopoly and anti-dumping;
(6) other circumstances that shall be determined as mandatory provisions.
